# Old Mac Donald - Engels kinderlied
# Traditioneel; de vorm met het refrein verscheen voor het eerst gedrukt in Tommy's
# Tunes (Londen, 1917), de naam Old MacDonald en de gangbare wijs in Amerikaanse
# opnamen uit 1927 (Wikipedia, en; de Morgan Library).
# Publiek domein.
# Overgenomen uit OLDMACDO.NAL (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991), dat ook een bewegingsversie
# (old-mac-donald-andere-versie) en een Nederlandse versie (old-mac-donald-nederlands)
# bevat. Na het eerste couplet geeft de bron per dier alleen twee regels, met
# "....."; zo overgenomen. Akkoorden bij het eerste couplet, naar de kolommen van de
# bron; Ami7 als Am7 geschreven.
{title: Old Mac Donald}
{meta: id old-mac-donald}
{meta: language en}
{lyricist: traditioneel}
{composer: traditioneel}
{copyright: Public domain}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: source Overgenomen uit OLDMACDO.NAL (WordPerfect 5.1, 1991), Engelse versie; herkomst via Wikipedia (en) en de Morgan Library}
{meta: tag kinderlied}
{meta: variant-group old-mac-donald}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Old [C]mac donald [G]had a farm
hia [D]hia [G]ho
[G]And on this farm he [C]had some [G]chicks
hia [D]hia [G]ho
[C]With a chick chick here [Am7]and a chick [Bbdim]chick [G]there
[C]Here a chick, there a [G]chick, ev'ry where [Am7]a chick chick.[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some cows
With a moow moow here and a moow moow there .....
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some bees
With a bzzz bzzz here .......
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some ducks
With a quack quack here .......
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some dogs
With a woof woof here ........
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some cats
With a miau miau here .......
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some mice
With a squeek squeek here ........
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some pigs
With a oink oink here .........
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some sheep
With a meh meh here ........
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some donkeys
With a ia ia here ........
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had some turkeys
With a gobble gobble here ........
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And on this farm he had a Ford
With a rattle rattle here ........
{end_of_verse}
